{"id": "31227", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=31227", "title": "San Lorenzo (Argentina)", "text": "San Lorenzo is a town near Salta, Argentina. The town is very green and home to a lot of nature, and is an easy day trip from Salta.\nGet in.\nYou can take the 7E bus from Salta. It costs $7 (November 2017), and the fare must be paid by transit card. If you don't have a Salta transit card, just get on the bus and find another passenger who will let you give them the cash and use their card."}
