{"id": "31255", "revid": "2310888", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=31255", "title": "San Mart\u00edn", "text": "San Mart\u00edn is the region of Peru that includes the department of San Martin. This is a region in northern Peru. Most of the department is located in the upper part of the Peruvian Amazon rainforest.\nEat.\nThe main typical dishes are:\nDrink.\nThe most common typical drinks are: masato, aguardiente, ventisho, seven roots, uvachado, chuchuhuasi, chapo, strong chicha, and courtsachados."}
{"id": "31259", "revid": "144844", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=31259", "title": "San Martin de los Andes", "text": "San Mart\u00edn de los Andes is a city in the Neuquen province in Argentina, it is on the edge of the Patagonian Andes mountains beside the L\u00e1car lake. It is a charming town that is a popular recreational destination because of the lake, nearby parks, and winter skiing at nearby Cerro Chapelco.\nUnderstand.\nSan Martin de los Andes is home to the quartermaster of Lanin National Park, one of the most important protected areas in Argentina. The city of San Martin de los Andes offers a wide range of accommodation, with an architecture based on prevailing local materials of stone and wood. The warmth in the decorations, the attention to every detail and personalized attention. Large windows, logs in household stoves, aromas and crafts pleasantly surprised visitors at each of the environments, and everything comes together to provide warmth and comfort in a unique natural environment. The accommodation consists of five star Hotels, Hosterias (lodges) and Caba\u00f1as - Apart hotel (cabins) are distributed harmonically taking advantage of the natural environment, combining the beauty of it with care landscaping. The population of San Martin de los Andes is estimated at 31,000 inhabitants. Its natural environment, allows the development of outdoor activities including fishing, hiking, camping, climbing, rafting, ecotourism, among many others.\nGet in.\nBy plane.\nAeropuerto Chapelco - Aviador Carlos Campos (') is the local airport. It is served by Aerolineas Argentinas and JetSMART with daily flights from Buenos Aires Jorge Newbury Aeroparque ('). The flight takes about 2 hours. Van transfers and taxis are available to and from the airport. \nBy car.\nYou can get in from Bariloche (4 hours, 60 pesos), Villa la Angostura or Neuqu\u00e9n.\nBy bus.\nSeveral bus companies in major cities throughout Argentina offer routes to San Martin de los Andes."}
