{"id": "31467", "revid": "144844", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=31467", "title": "San Teodoro (Mindoro)", "text": "San Teodoro is a municipality in Oriental Mindoro. It's a quiet place, out of the way of the bustling night-life and commerce of Puerto Galera and Sabang.\nGet in.\nSeveral ferry lines go to Puerto Galera and Calapan from Batangas. Prices are \u20b1150-200 per person. It might be worth while to check how long the ride will take, and also the size of the boat, especially if the weather is less than perfect.\nThere are also Ro-Ro ferries, if you want to bring a car. Depending on size, \u20b11000-1200.\nWhen in Mindoro, jeepney's go regularly between Calapan and Puerto Galera. As always in rural Philippines, jeepneys will be packed to the limit, including people on the roof. For a more comfortable ride, rent a van (\u20b12000-2500 for the day, including driver) or arrange a pick up from your hotel.\nThe trip from either Puerto Galera or Calapan is around 30 min by car and 1 hour by jeepney (they stop, frequently).\nGet around.\nBy jeepney (Puerto Galera - Calapan) or car/van (rent or arrange via your hotel)\nDo.\nOne of San Teodoro's charms is that there's \"really nothing to do\". \nBut if it gets too quiet you can swim in one of the above-mentioned falls. In Tamaraw Falls there's man-made pools on the mountain side (entrance \u20b125/person), in Tukuban there's natural pools in the forest. The last stretch going to Tukuban includes a hike or carabao ride (\u20b1350 for up to six people) across several streams.\nRiver Kayaking can be arranged, ask your hotel.\nDive or snorkel. The snorkeling is not as good as in Puerto Galera, so you might want to rent a boat (banka).\nBuy.\nAgain, San Teodoro is the place to get away from the vendors. Nevertheless, some handicraft from the local Mangyan tribe are available.\nEat.\nRed Sail Resto Bar serves international and local cuisine. Prices vary from \u20b170-400.\nSleep.\n(Contact number Rica Ra\u00f1on, +63 918-691 1726, Jay Ra\u00f1on +63 918-375 4456).\nFamily Room or Honeymoon Suite for \u20b12500/night, including breakfast.\nStandard Room for \u20b11500/night, excluding breakfast.\nAll rooms have air-con and cable TV.\nThere is also a children's playroom available, free of charge."}
{"id": "31468", "revid": "43226", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=31468", "title": "San Teodoro (Sardinia)", "text": "San Teodoro, the southern doorway to Sardinia's \"Emerald Coast\", is 25 km from Olbia.\nSee.\nSan Teodoro coastline is characterized by impressive beaches and bays. The most famous beach (not only in Sardinia but in Italy too) is La Cinta. From there you can admire San Teodoro's lagoon with its vegetation and its fauna, including pink flamingos. Very beautiful too is Cala Brandinchi, another popular beach known also as Tahiti for its exotic appearance. \nDo.\nOn Tavolara Island, part of the Tavolara and Punta Coda Cavallo Marine Preserve, there is the VLF transmitter ICV, which is used for transmitting submarines on the frequencies 20.26 kHz and 20.76 kHz to submerged submarines. It uses as antenna a span between two mountains and is surely an interesting facility for people, who like towers and spans, but it may be situated, because of its military use in restricted area and may be only admirable from far away. The island is off the coast about 15 km north of San Teodoro."}
